WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:01.130 --> 00:03.300
Hey Leila, how are you doing?

2
00:03.300 --> 00:07.710
Hey Nate, not great to be honest.
This round of layoffs is making me nervous.

3
00:08.230 --> 00:10.240
I can relate. It's a stressful time.

4
00:11.140 --> 00:12.390
Are you looking at other jobs?

5
00:12.870 --> 00:15.140
I'm trying, but I haven't had much luck.

6
00:15.590 --> 00:18.790
I need to find a different job
where I won't be as replaceable.

7
00:19.270 --> 00:22.270
All my experience has been
in customer service, unfortunately.

8
00:22.600 --> 00:25.890
I have no idea what employers
are even looking for.

9
00:26.410 --> 00:29.600
The last time I was shifting careers,
my former manager recommended

10
00:29.600 --> 00:33.090
that I proactively sign up for courses
and certifications to learn different skill sets.

11
00:33.860 --> 00:36.230
That's interesting.
What kind of skills did you learn?

12
00:36.970 --> 00:40.070
Everything ranging from thinking critically
to structuring my communication.

13
00:40.810 --> 00:44.710
These skills are crucial to any career,
and typically what most employers are looking for.

14
00:45.480 --> 00:48.640
And why you have to learn other skills,
which can certainly be challenging.

15
00:49.250 --> 00:51.870
Keeping your successes in mind
can help you through the tough times.

16
00:52.490 --> 00:53.790
This is very helpful.

17
00:54.150 --> 00:59.390
I did see an opening for a computer user support
specialist that would allow me to work remotely,

18
00:59.880 --> 01:01.380
but I'm hesitant to apply.

19
01:02.020 --> 01:02.950
Why is that?

20
01:03.210 --> 01:07.500
To be honest, I feel overwhelmed
and slightly resentful towards technology.

21
01:07.500 --> 01:12.000
It seems like it's always changing
and I can never keep up.

22
01:12.930 --> 01:17.380
Learning how you can work and think in new ways with
data and technology will not only remove barriers,

23
01:17.830 --> 01:20.600
but it will put you in a great place
to apply for this role.

24
01:20.930 --> 01:23.810
Of course, you'll need to continue
expanding your digital skills,

25
01:24.450 --> 01:26.500
but a good foundation will get you
started to keep learning.
